From d0cd6ad321429589c03b7f5f88400359cc98932d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doug Gabehart <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:10:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: add GGML_OP_SSM_CONV_SPLIT (CPU+Vulkan) to skip the
 per-layer conv-state concat

delta-net-base.cpp's build_conv_state materialized concat(prefix, new_tokens)
before every ggml_ssm_conv call in the qwen35/qwen35moe/qwen3next GDN path --
a full-size copy on every layer just to satisfy ggml_ssm_conv's single-buffer
contract. GGML_OP_SSM_CONV_SPLIT takes the two pieces directly (prefix always
contiguous, new_tokens a possibly non-contiguous transposed view) and reads
across the split itself, so the concat is no longer needed.

Scoped to CPU and Vulkan only -- the two backends this fleet actually runs --
not the ~11 other ggml_ssm_conv backends or the non-delta-net call sites
(lfm2.cpp, mtmd audio). The tail-rows state-save logic in build_conv_state,
which used to slice the concatenated buffer, is reworked into a small bounded
window (build_conv_window) that straddles the prefix/new_tokens boundary only
when it actually needs to (n_t < d_conv - 1, i.e. during decode).

New op appended at the end of ggml_op (not grouped next to SSM_CONV) to avoid
shifting every later op's wire value for ggml-rpc's version-checked protocol,
and given a case in ggml-backend-meta.cpp's split-state switch so a future
LLAMA_SPLIT_MODE_TENSOR user doesn't hit an unhandled-op abort (untested
against real multi-device execution -- this fleet never uses that mode).

Verified: 90/90 test-backend-ops cases pass on CPU and Vulkan (contiguous and
transposed new_tokens, boundary and prefill-sized cases). Measured on
gabesrv10 (Radeon 8060S, production paused for exclusive GPU access):
Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q4_K_XL pp1024 255.9-251.9 t/s baseline -> 266.6-267.1 t/s
modified (~4-5%, matches the fleet profiling report's predicted ~4.4%).
GGML_VK_PERF_LOGGER confirms the per-layer CONCAT (214.6ms/pass baseline) is
gone entirely in the modified build.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5
